         Home  > Registering To Vote          Registering To Vote      




			 The first step in voting is registering. This page has all of the information you need to determine if you are eligible to vote and walks you through the registration process step-by-step. 






			 Register to Vote 
 Voters have three options to register to vote. 

 Register  online  to vote 
 Print out a voter registration form and mail it to our office 
 Register at the polls 

  Military or overseas (UOCAVA) voters can visit  FVAP.gov  to register and request a ballot. 



  Register to Vote Online  Download Voter Registration Form 


			 If you choose to download the Voter Registration Form, you can fill out the form, print it and send it to our office. 
 Send Voter Registration Forms to: 
 Ada County Elections 
400 N Benjamin Ln, Ste 100 
Boise ID 83704 








 Register/Update Your Registration 




 You’ll need to register to vote or update your registration if you have not registered or if you have  changed your name or address.  To use the online voter registration system, you will need a current Idaho driver’s license or  free identification card. 










 Check your Registration 




 If you are unsure about your voter information, visit the  online voter registration system  to check and ensure your information is accurate. 








			 Qualifications to Register 
 To vote in the next election, you must meet all of the requirements below. Please keep in mind, that Idahoans can register to vote in advance of the election or when they show up to vote at the polls. Please review the  requirements.  

 You must be 18 by Election Day 
 You must be a U.S. Citizen 
 You must have lived in Ada County for 30 days prior to Election Day 
 Provide valid photo identification (current Idaho state-issued ID, current tribal card, current U.S. passport or current Idaho Concealed Weapons license) 
 You must provide either a state ID number or the last four digits of your social security number 
 You must provide  proof of residency  (current utility bill, bank statement, etc.) 
 Felons may not register until they have completed the terms of their sentence 







			 Designate a Political Party 
 When you register to vote, you have the option to affiliate with a political party. However, voters may change or declare their party affiliation by completing the form below and mailing it to our office or emailing to  [email protected] . 



  Download Party Affiliation form 


			 Canceling Voter Registration 
 To cancel your voter registration, please fill out and return the  Voter Registration Cancellation  form. To confirm your registration status, please visit  VoteIdaho.gov  or contact our office. 






			 Have Questions About Elections? 
 Check out our  Frequently Asked Questions. 






























